  "query_preview": "..\nA boundary of converging winds from the west and northeast has lined \nup over Guam, resulting in scattered showers and isolated \nthunderstorms early this evening that could spread to Rota in the \nnext few hours. A similar boundary will move over Saipan and Tinian \naround midnight, leading to scattered showers and isolated \nthunderstorms that will continue through Friday. Afterwards, a weak \ncirculation embedded within the monsoon trough currently west of the \nregion will invigorate showers and convection mainly over Guam and \nRota into the weekend. Model guidance indicates this circulation \nquickly passing through the Marianas and heading north, so isolated \nshower coverage may return to the southern islands towards the end of\nthe weekend. As for Saipan and Tinian, drier air ahead of Tropical \nStorm Koguma (27W) may be enough to keep these islands in isolated \nshower coverage from Friday night on. Afterwards, benign weather\nconditions are possible next week.",
